BND-14: reject a subcatchment that drains onto a subcatchment with no area

subcatch_readParams() accepts an Area of 0. Runoff sent to such a
subcatchment is dropped by subcatch_addRunonFlow(), the zero-area
subcatchment is skipped by runoff_execute(), and the upstream runoff is not
counted as leaving the study area because its outlet is a subcatchment, so
the water disappears without a message. subcatch_validate() now reports a
new ERROR 106 for a subcatchment with area that drains onto a subcatchment
without area. The error number is new; it is unused in 5.2.4, 5.3.0 and
6.0.0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-14_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/error.h b/src/legacy/engine/error.h
index 2bcea19..5cdff02 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/error.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/error.h
@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@ enum ErrorType {
 // ... Subcatchment/Aquifer Errors
       /*! \brief Subcatchment has no outlet */
       ERR_SUBCATCH_OUTLET      = 108,
+      /*! \brief Subcatchment drains onto a subcatchment with no area */
+      ERR_SUBCATCH_NO_AREA     = 106,
       /*! \brief Aquifer parameter error */
       ERR_AQUIFER_PARAMS       = 109,
       /*! \brief Ground elevation error */
